        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): clamp restart drain timers when deferral is oversized",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSafe gateway restarts can accept an oversized `gateway.reload.deferralTimeoutMs` value, but Node timers cannot represent delays above the platform-safe maximum. Without clamping, restart drain waits can arm overflowing timers and force the restart path before the configured drain budget is actually honored.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis keeps the restart drain budget inside the existing Node-safe timer contract at the restart resolver boundary, then applies the same timer-safe normalization in the two process-level drain waiters that can also be called directly. The change preserves `0` as the indefinite/immediate sentinel for the existing restart paths, preserves positive fractional `waitForActiveTasks` behavior by clamping it to a real timer, and does not add config, schema, protocol, or provider behavior.\n\nThis is AI-assisted.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators who configure a very large restart deferral budget get a bounded, timer-safe drain instead of an early timeout caused by Node timer overflow.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: oversized safe-restart drain budgets and direct process drain waiter timeouts clamp to `MAX_TIMER_TIMEOUT_MS`, while zero/indefinite and positive fractional wait behavior stay intact.\n- Focused proof at `c8597646e498365fab7c086df3e2fcf083d54819`: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/process/gateway-work-admission.test.ts src/process/command-queue.test.ts` passed with 55 tests.\n- Focused proof at `c8597646e498365fab7c086df3e2fcf083d54819`: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/restart.test.ts -t resolveGatewayRestartDeferralTimeoutMs` passed with 1 selected test.\n- Current head `24f5cd51b60cf2a94b5ff464654946e9b0b2b619`: merging latest `upstream/main` did not change the six timer files from the focused-proof head.\n- Current-head CI at `24f5cd51b60cf2a94b5ff464654946e9b0b2b619`: `check-lint` passed in GitHub Actions run `29257531777` / job `86841857324`.\n- Current-head diff hygiene at `24f5cd51b60cf2a94b5ff464654946e9b0b2b619`: `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Observed result: restart deferral resolution, root-work drain waits, and active-task drain waits now use the shared Node-safe timer maximum for oversized finite values.",
